I feel obliged to send a hearty thank-you to the folks who hosted the 
tournament, and coded all of the scripts for the trophies and other 
statistics.

I walked into the tournament having only heard rumour of the Quest level 
and the Castle and so on.  With high hopes of a bronze star, tofumage 
the often Valkyrie headed into the Dungeons of Doom.  (senon's insolent 
minx took out my first incarnation.  I think it could smell the 
Gauntlets of Power and was offended!)

My second-to-last attempt got as far as the beginning of the Valley of 
the Dead and seemed quite likely to go further, but became the victim of 
an odd crash, disintegrating without a trace on the server.

At any rate, the carrot of the tournament was enough to provide me the 
patience to discover that the Quest and Medusa and the Castle are not 
group hallucinations of the r.g.r.n -- or at least that a lurker can 
catch it, too!  I'm hoping to be able to post a YAFAP between now and 
next November, so I can aim more realistically for a trophy of some sort.

So thanks to all who were involved.  The month was a blast.

Congrats to everyone who won trophies.  You've certainly earned them!

